    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "H1SUM2",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the full adder: sum stage of half adder 1 (chain 2 of 4), Y = A XOR B; the four duplicated chains carry the partial sum onto the four operand pins of half adder 2 (H2N1A.B, H2N1B.B, H2N3.B, H2N5.B) \u2014 one waveguide per pin, so the textbook shared stage is instantiated four times. The whole full adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of A, B and Cin onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_e512f26d9ce54d4b807e0bdbc6d2ca8b",
        "IdGuid": "688354b3-2448-4ab7-bff9-bf02c6ed3530",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "67901253-a45a-463f-a72f-38a979d860e2",
          "32d54943-2440-4188-ad29-ad1504fed742",
